// Reactive `for`s along a tree follow their events where the tree has
// links: from a node with an event up to its parent (a trigger on a
// child's, from the leaves), down to its children, and on to the sibling
// after it (a trigger on the sibling before's), each passing on what its
// body changed (or added into its parent); the nodes without a parent
// are come to by their rows, and a node that has other children or
// siblings than before is come to itself.
// Inputs/tree_follow.ent works a wide tree out that way and, without
// triggers, by going through all of it, in every frame of forty in which
// sizes change, the order of siblings, a leaf goes and a node moves with
// all under it: the two never disagree. (Leaving out any one of the
// marks that following sets makes them disagree.)
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/tree_follow.ent \
// RUN:     -I %S/../../devices -o %t.mlir
// RUN: ent-opt %t.mlir "--ent-lower-to-loops=explain=1" -o /dev/null 2>&1 \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EXPLAIN

// Both the `for` from the leaves and the one from the roots.
// EXPLAIN:     remark: follows its events along the tree
// EXPLAIN:     leaves first
// EXPLAIN:     remark: follows its events along the tree
// EXPLAIN-NOT: goes through its whole tree

// CHECK-NOT:  wrong {{[1-9]}}
// CHECK:      1: wrong 0 runs 979
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: wrong 0 runs 450
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: wrong 0 runs 66
// Nothing changed: nothing ran.
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: wrong 0 runs 0
// CHECK:      40: wrong 0 runs 228
